    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d334-a1">

                <pb facs="0466" n="386" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg386"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Komura Jutaro to Mr. Buck.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-12-05"><hi rendition="#italic">December 5,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge
                    the receipt of your excellency’s note dated the 20th ultimo, expressing through
                    me to the minister for the navy your high appreciation and thanks for two
                    Japanese vessels having been dispatched to the assistance of the United States
                    transport <hi rendition="#italic">Hancock</hi>, aground near Moji, and at the
                    same time desiring that the bill of expenses for the two vessels be made
                    known.</p>
                <p>Having at once communicated to the minister for the navy upon the subject, I am
                    now in receipt of a reply from him requesting me to state that he profoundly
                    appreciates your excellency’s courtesy, but that the expenses for the said
                    vessels are not expected to be refunded.</p>
                <p>I avail, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Komura Jutaro</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Minister for Foreign Affairs.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
